From 277235d959a7b77d419c52a3e67533c0d9e38f4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:04:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] backends/color: Refresh preferred targets after output
 topology changes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A surface that is not on any output gets the primary output's
description as its preferred description. When only the topology
changed (another output became primary, or the primary was removed)
no color device emitted a change, so such surfaces kept the old
primary's description.

Recompute every output's description record when the Wayland outputs
are updated, publish all changed output descriptions first, and then
re-evaluate the preferred description of every surface, so that no
surface is pointed at a target that has not been published yet. A
target range whose minimum is not below its whole-cd/m² maximum is now
rejected too, since it would publish an empty range.

The target-luminance test now also switches the primary output and
removes it, and the test client accounts for forced HDR being global:
toggling it changes every output's description, not only the one under
test.

Related: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/5001
---
